    "operator": "Stop only when the running sum is STRICTLY GREATER THAN x, instead of at least x. Time remains zero-based and -1 still denotes an infinite run.",
    "correctness_argument": "Let S be a full-cycle sum and M the maximum first-cycle prefix. If x>M and S<=0, the threshold is never reached; otherwise the earliest feasible cycle is max(0,ceil((x-M)/S)). Binary search first-cycle prefix maxima for the residual target. The independent oracle considers EVERY prefix position i and computes the first feasible cycle at that position, minimizing cycle*n+i using 128-bit intermediate arithmetic. L3 changes the integer threshold to x+1.",
